1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. exd5 { White abruptly switches to an Exchange French structure where he commits to Nc3 and Black to ... Bb4. What is the significance of this? Well, this means that when White later plays a2-a3, Black will probably hand over the bishop-pair with ... Bxc3+, since retreating the bishop results in the loss of a tempo. Now we do get something for the swap:
1. White is the one who lost a tempo inducing the swap with a2-a3.
2. After the swap White’s queenside pawn structure has been damaged. } 4... exd5 5. Bd3 Nc6 6. a3 (6. Ne2 Nge7 7. O-O Bf5 8. Ng3 Bxd3 9. Qxd3 Qd7 10. a3 Bxc3 11. Qxc3 O-O-O 12. b4 Rde8 13. b5 Nd8 14. a4 h5) 6... Bxc3+ 7. bxc3 Nge7 8. Qh5 Be6 9. Ne2 Qd7 10. O-O Bf5 *


