1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 c5 { The Tarrasch may well be White’s safest French.
To this day I still can’t find even a trace of an edge for White in this version
if Black plays correctly. If the 4 ... Qxd5 line contains within it a flaw for Black, then it is its drawish nature. I find it difficult to beat lower-rated players with it. But when you have the black pieces, we can’t expect to start the game with an advantage either, so for me it’s the best line Black has at our disposal. } *


