1. e4 e6 2. Qe2 Nf6 3. e5 { With a single move the idea of a King’s Indian Attack goes by the wayside
and the position looks more like an Alekhine’s Defence } 3... Nd5 4. d4 (4. c4 { Possible too } 4... Nb6 5. d4 d5! 6. c5 N6d7 7. Qc2 c6 8. b4 b6 9. a3 a5 10. Bb2 f6 $10 { [%cal Gc8a6] }) 4... c5 5. Nf3 (5. c4 Nb4 6. dxc5 (6. a3?? Qa5! 7. Bd2 Nc2+ 8. Kd1 Qa4!) 6... Bxc5 7. a3 Qa5 8. Nc3 Bd4 9. Nf3 N8c6 10. Qe4 Bxc3+ 11. bxc3 Na6 $15) 5... Nc6 6. dxc5! (6. c3?! { looks like a line out of the c3-Sicilian where White decided to play the absurd Qe2. } 6... cxd4 7. Nxd4 (7. cxd4 Qb6) 7... Nxd4 8. cxd4 Qa5+ 9. Bd2 Qb6 $15) 6... Bxc5 7. g3 O-O 8. Bg2 f6 9. c4 Nb6 10. O-O fxe5 11. Nxe5 Nd4! $10 12. Qd1! { White must sacrifice his c-pawn } (12. Qd3?! Qf6 13. Ng4 Qf5! 14. Qxf5 exf5 15. Ne3 Ne2+ 16. Kh1 f4 17. gxf4 Nxf4 $17) 12... d6 13. Nd3 Nxc4 14. Nxc5 dxc5 *


