1. e4 e6 2. b3 d5 3. Bb2 Nf6 { In this version we refuse to get sucked into White’s gambit and insist on a
real French position } 4. e5 { White’s most dynamic move } (4. exd5 exd5 { Yes, another obnoxious delayed Exchange Variation is reached } 5. Nf3 Be7 6. Be2 O-O 7. O-O Bg4 (7... c5 { more dynamic is to take on an isolani position } 8. d4 Nc6) 8. d4) 4... Nfd7 5. d4 c5 6. c3 Nc6 7. Nd2 f6 8. f4 b6!? { A new idea. Black plans to fianchetto and eventually castle long } 9. Bd3 { [%cal Gd1h5] } 9... Qe7 { 9 ... f5 is also an idea. } 10. a3 Bb7 11. Qh5+ Qf7 12. Qxf7+ Kxf7 $10 { Chances look even to me in this ending, since White’s space ‘advantage’ is
offset by his potential to overextend. } *


